    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "(We consider $ \\hat{u} - u $ rather than $ \\hat{u} $ as the latter includes variance from both the prediction error and the random effects u themselves.) The standard errors of the fixed and random effects are obtained, respectively, as the square roots of the diagonal elements of $ C_{11} $ and $ C_{22} $. For very large animal breeding designs where the inverse of the MME matrix may be difficult to compute, Meyer (1989a) presents methods for approximating the diagonal elements of the inverse of this matrix (and hence the standard errors).",
